              > catches when implementation diverges from the spec. Fix the spec, or record the drift with
              <span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;color:#C9E8ED;"
                >moment sync propose</span
              > and accept or reject each proposal.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight:600; font-size:16.5px; margin-bottom:10px; color:#E6F0F2;">
              Can I adopt incrementally?
            </div>
            <p style="margin:0; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.6; color:#90A2AA;">
              Yes. Start with one bounded context. Moment generates artifacts alongside your existing
              code, context by context, aggregate by aggregate.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight:600; font-size:16.5px; margin-bottom:10px; color:#E6F0F2;">
              How mature is it?
            </div>
            <p style="margin:0; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.6; color:#90A2AA;">
              Pre-1.0 and in active development. The current release is {MOMENT_VERSION}. The
              pipeline runs end to end, and all 11 packages, from the parser to the board and the
              MCP server, are published on npm under <span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;color:#C9E8ED;"
                >@mmmnt</span
              > and versioned together. Minor releases can still change the language. Each one ships
              a changelog.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight:600; font-size:16.5px; margin-bottom:10px; color:#E6F0F2;">
              Do I need to know DDD?
            </div>
            <p style="margin:0; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.6; color:#90A2AA;">
              Basic familiarity with aggregates, commands, and events helps, but the DSL reads like a
              domain description, not an academic paper.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight:600; font-size:16.5px; margin-bottom:10px; color:#E6F0F2;">
              What about the license?
            </div>
            <p style="margin:0; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.6; color:#90A2AA;">
              FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0: source-available now with full read and use rights. Two years after
              each release it converts to Apache 2.0. The only FSL-period restriction is competing
              commercial use.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* FINAL CTA */}
    <section style="position:relative; border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);">
      <div
        style="position:absolute; bottom:-80px; left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%); width:1000px; height:420px; background:radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(34,211,238,0.12), transparent 70%); pointer-events:none;"
      >
      </div>
      <div
        class="site-container"
        style="position:relative; max-width:1200px; margin:0 auto; padding:96px 40px; text-align:center;"
      >
        <h2
          style="font-weight:600; font-size:50px; line-height:1.06; letter-spacing:-.02em; margin:0 0 18px; color:#F2FBFC;"
        >
          Rehearse before you build.
        </h2>
        <p style="font-size:18px; color:#90A2AA; max-width:500px; margin:0 auto 34px;">
          Version {MOMENT_VERSION} on npm. Eleven packages and an MCP server. Source-available under
          FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex; gap:14px; justify-content:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a
            href="/get-started"
            class="btn-primary"
            style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600; padding:14px 28px; border-radius:8px;"
            >Get started</a
          >
          <a
            href={GITHUB_URL}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="btn-secondary"
            style="font-size:15px; font-weight:500; padding:14px 24px; border-radius:8px;"
            >Star on GitHub</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Footer />
  </div>

  <script>
    // Homepage hero — animate commit/reveal beats when the tab is visible.
    // Reduced-motion users see the final composed state without animation.
    class MomHeroAnim {
      root: HTMLElement | null;
      played = false;
      timers: number[] = [];
      onVis: () => void;

      constructor() {
        this.root = document.getElementById('momHero');
        this.onVis = () => {
          if (document.visibilityState === 'visible' && !this.played) this.play();
        };
      }

      mount() {
        if (!this.root) return;
        if (document.visibilityState === 'visible') {
          window.setTimeout(() => this.play(), 400);
        } else {
          document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', this.onVis);
        }
        const replay = document.getElementById('momReplay');
        if (replay) replay.addEventListener('click', () => this.play(true));
      }

      play(force = false) {
        const root = this.root;
        if (!root) return;
        const reduce = window.matchMedia?.('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        if (reduce && !force) {
          this.played = true;
          return;
        }
        this.played = true;
        this.timers.forEach((t) => clearTimeout(t));
        this.timers = [];
        const nodes = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-kind]'));
        nodes.forEach((n) => {
          const k = n.dataset.kind;
          if (k === 'commit') {
            n.style.opacity = '0.32';
            n.style.borderLeftColor = 'transparent';
            n.style.background = 'transparent';
          } else if (k === 'reveal') {
            n.style.opacity = '0.28';
          } else {
            n.style.opacity = '0';
          }
        });
        nodes.forEach((n) => {
          const k = n.dataset.kind;
          const d = parseInt(n.dataset.delay ?? '0', 10) || 0;
          this.timers.push(
            window.setTimeout(() => {
              if (k === 'commit') {
                n.style.opacity = '1';
                n.style.borderLeftColor = 'rgba(34,211,238,0.55)';
                n.style.background = 'rgba(34,211,238,0.16)';
                this.timers.push(
                  window.setTimeout(() => {
                    n.style.background = 'rgba(34,211,238,0.05)';
                  }, 360),
                );
              } else if (k === 'reveal') {
                n.style.opacity = '0.92';
              } else {
                n.style.opacity = '1';
              }
            }, d),
          );
        });
        const pulse = document.getElementById('momPulsePath') as unknown as SVGAnimateMotionElement | null;
        if (pulse && 'beginElement' in pulse) {
          this.timers.push(
            window.setTimeout(() => {
              try {
                pulse.beginElement();
              } catch {}
            }, 2900),
          );
        }
      }
    }

    new MomHeroAnim().mount();
  </script>
</Base>
